# nr-tui-sv-store: what the lead applies (nothing here is applied by the task)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-session-view/Cargo.toml (the file belongs to nr-tui-protocol-audit; the store needs more than it declares)

[dependencies]: replace the `tokio` line (anchor: `tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["sync"] }`) with
tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["sync", "rt", "macros"] }
and add, after `mixdog-js = { workspace = true }` (anchor: that line):
# The store's timers (first-state wait, section wait, the sign-in poll, the exit wait) go through mixdog_rt::time, as the client's do.
mixdog-rt = { workspace = true }

Add a [dev-dependencies] table at the end of the file (tests/store_mock.rs):
[dev-dependencies]
async-trait = { workspace = true }
tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "macros", "sync"] }

## native/core/Cargo.lock (offline, --locked)

The `[[package]] name = "mixdog-session-view"` entry gains the dependencies "async-trait" and "mixdog-rt" (both crates are already in the lock file and in the workspace; no new crate). The tokio features add nothing to the lock file.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack

Regenerate the hack for the new tokio features of mixdog-session-view ("rt", "macros") as for any feature change of a member.

## mixdog-app-server-daemon/src/compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING

Nothing to remove: this task registers no service and adds no protocol method (every request the store sends is a method the protocol already has).

## For the tasks after this one

- mixdog-tui, mixdog-repl: call mixdog_launch::ensure_core, then `SessionStore::connect(StoreOptions { .. })` (or `connect::connect_with(connector, options)` over their own connector); they drive `SessionStore::tick()` once per terminal frame, read `state()`, and take `subscribe()` events (State, Notice, Toast, ConnectionStatus, UiOpenRequest, PromptRestore, SessionLost). They call `dispose(reason)` on exit (it waits at most EXIT_WAIT = 2500 ms and answers whether it finished).
- The palette stays in the UI process: apply it locally first, then `mirror_theme(id, options)` (setTheme with persist false, failure ignored).
- tests/store_core.rs (the store against an in-process core) is not written: see the result of nr-tui-sv-store.
